1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:07,880
Most DAOs vote on Snapshot, off chain, and a Safe multisig
carries out the result on chain. Nothing checks that what the

2
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:15,260
signers executed is what token holders voted for. This is
AsVoted, running on GenLayer. Every figure on this page is read

3
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:20,530
from the contracts: fifteen real executions checked, ten as
voted, two that deviate, three unclear.

4
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:29,509
Here is one check. On the left, the ballot: the Velora proposal
to return 40.203 wrapped ether to Bybit after the hack, fetched

5
00:00:29,509 --> 00:00:37,666
by its IPFS hash and verified inside the contract. On the right,
the receipt: the Safe execution, read from two independent RPCs

6
00:00:37,666 --> 00:00:40,261
that must agree, decoded action by action.

7
00:00:40,711 --> 00:00:47,282
The recipient and the amount are both written in the proposal,
so code settles this action. No model is involved. The verdict

8
00:00:47,282 --> 00:00:48,182
is as voted.

9
00:00:48,628 --> 00:00:55,899
Check seven is a CoW DAO batch of four calls. Two of them are
quoted in the proposal, calldata for calldata, and code

10
00:00:55,899 --> 00:01:02,537
authorizes them. The other two call a contract that CIP-16 never
names. The ruling is worded neutrally and dated: the execution

11
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:05,066
includes an action the proposal does not mention.

12
00:01:05,516 --> 00:01:12,878
When the data cannot settle it, the answer is unclear, never a
guess. This ParaSwap grant was set at five hundred dollars per

13
00:01:12,878 --> 00:01:18,000
epoch and paid in PSP. The contract never fetches prices, so it
does not compare them.

14
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:25,461
Code decides first: every address, every amount summed across
transfers, every delegate call. A model only reads calls the

15
00:01:25,461 --> 00:01:32,473
proposal describes in words, it must quote the proposal
verbatim, and two answers must agree. It never decides an

16
00:01:32,473 --> 00:01:35,794
address, an amount, a chain fact, or the verdict.

17
00:01:36,244 --> 00:01:41,853
The demo registry runs the same code with ninety second windows,
so every path can be shown end to end.

18
00:01:42,303 --> 00:01:50,059
A real story from choosing seeds. CoW DAO sent 67 wrapped ether
to its treasury. Filed against CIP-43, which states 60 ether, it

19
00:01:50,059 --> 00:01:57,814
ruled deviates. But the transfer went to the treasury, not from
it. The DAO appealed with a bond and named CIP-28, the mandate

20
00:01:57,814 --> 00:02:03,884
to send profits to the treasury. A fresh validator panel ruled
as voted, and the bond was refunded.

21
00:02:04,334 --> 00:02:10,657
When a deviates ruling becomes final, the DAO's pledge is
slashed by a frozen severity table, and the slash is paid to

22
00:02:10,657 --> 00:02:15,830
whoever proved it. Every state has a deadline and an exit anyone
can call. There is no owner.

23
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:23,555
Other contracts can ask one question: is this DAO executing as
voted? This small consumer refused to act after the final

24
00:02:23,555 --> 00:02:25,287
deviates ruling, and logged why.

25
00:02:25,737 --> 00:02:27,460
Back on the canonical registry.

26
00:02:27,910 --> 00:02:35,171
A patrol bot runs every fifteen minutes. It watches every listed
Safe, matches each new execution to the latest passed proposal

27
00:02:35,171 --> 00:02:40,702
that names something it touches, files the check, and closes its
own filings after their deadlines.

28
00:02:41,152 --> 00:02:47,573
Anyone can verify the deployment. This page reads each
contract's code back from Studio Dev and hashes it against the

29
00:02:47,573 --> 00:02:54,315
deploy commit on GitHub, in your browser. The books balance on
both registries, and the demo has drained to exactly zero.

30
00:02:54,765 --> 00:02:58,942
Every filing, ruling and payout is a transaction on the GenLayer
explorer.

31
00:02:59,392 --> 00:03:05,554
AsVoted. The ballot and the receipt, read by the chain, held
side by side, with money behind the answer.
